WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.550 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  venom has arrived and the public just  can't seem to get enough of the world's  most popular brain-eating alien symbiote  but while you were distracted by that  slippery slimy tongue you might have  missed some of the film's more subtle  moments  here's a look at some small details you  missed in venom  source material one thing is very clear  in almost every scene of venom  the people who made the movie are big  fans of the comic book  some of it is pretty obvious like the  fact that the life foundation was front  and center in a number of plot lines  involving the alien symbiotes  but there's plenty beyond that for  instance there's the idea that the life  foundation's original goal was to cure  cancer  that comes from the origin story of the  ultimate marvel universe's version of  venom  then there are specific sequences for  instance the scene where riot  rips venom out of eddie's host body is  an almost exact recreation of the cover  of venom carnage unleashed number three  and there are even specific lines of  dialogue borrowed from the comics like  the line  [Music]  which originally appeared in the pages  of amazing spider-man number 374  creator call outs venom features all  sorts of references to the writers and  artists who created the character  most prominently when eddie's  ex-girlfriend anne mentions the name of  her law firm  mkhilani and mcfarland those names of  course belong to writer david mcelini  and artist todd mcfarlane who co-created  venom in amazing spider-man number 299  but some references are more obscure  near eddie's chinatown apartment for  instance a sign in the background in the  final scene reads  ron lim's herbals which is a reference  to artist ron lim  who penciled the venom lethal protector  miniseries that much of the film is  based on  and the apartment building eddie lives  in that would be the shuler building  named for randy schuler a fan who sent  his idea for a black spiderman costume  to marvel in the 1980s inadvertently  providing the original inspiration for  venom in the first place  nice deadly doggy one of venom's many  funny moments is the all too brief  sequence in the hospital when  separated from eddie brock the venom  symbiote is forced to use a tiny little  doggie named gemini as a host in order  to survive  that's actually a subtle reference to  the comics where not one but  two dogs have been turned into symbiotic  monsters  one was ivan a sled dog while the other  was a german shepherd  named samson both symbiote dogs proved  that when it comes to pet ownership  good breeding does indeed matter so if  you suspect your pet has been bonded  with an alien killer  please consider getting it spayed or  neutered the symbiote scream  at the beginning of the film it's  mentioned that there are five  alien life forms being brought back to  earth one is venom  one is riot who bonds with the movie's  villain carlton drake  one is apparently agony the bluish  symbiote who kills poor doctor dora  skirth before dying itself  and one is probably carnage who may or  may not be attached to serial killer  cletus cassidy by the time the first  post-credit scene hits the screen  but there's also a fifth symbiote who  seemingly vanishes  way through the film the yellow symbiote  who briefly bonds with a super cute  little bunny rabbit  exactly which symbiote this is and what  happened to it are both mysteries but  while some speculate that the bunny  might have housed the symbiote known as  phage the smart money is on another  yellow tinted symbiote  scream in the comics both phage and  scream were created by the life  foundation but scream eventually turned  on the others and killed  all their host forms believing symbiotes  to be evil  given that the film seems to be setting  up venom versus carnage for the sequel  having a loose canon like scream at  large and looking to eliminate both of  them could be a fun  and interesting twist the wilhelm scream  it's not just comic book fans that got  serviced with in jokes  movie buffs also got their own call out  thanks to the prominent use of the  legendary wilhelm scream during the  scene where venom fights the swat team  the audio was actually first used way  back in 1951 for the film the distant  drums during a scene where a man was  eaten by an alligator  named for private wilhelm a character  who gives this pained cry in 1953's the  charge at feather river after being shot  by an arrow  the sound effect was revived in 1977  star wars when a storm trooper fell to  his doom  inside the death star it subsequently  became a tradition for star wars and  indiana jones films and then spread to  everything from reservoir dogs to beauty  and the beast  pretty exciting that venom is keeping  the tradition alive

